7961	{"artifactId":"LLD-fa396bdf197b8e8b-s1","entry":{"id":"review-2670c8e04dca1fb72fc045c0af73e4a2","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-27T06:00:03.188Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.1","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Treating a failed index request as fresh preserves the ISSUE's degraded-review escape when a changed file remains unindexed.","evidence":"ISSUE.md requires that the gate 'ends in the existing degraded diff review if they still do not become fresh'. The proposed attempted-and-idle rule instead clears staleness. handler.ts only degrades when 'g.grounding.symbols.length === 0'; grounding.ts omits entity-less files while retaining symbols from other changed files. A mixed set therefore proceeds to full review with the failed file absent from grounding. [files: docs/standalone/fix-code-review-freshness-gate-so-E20261027fa396bdf/ISSUE.md, src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/handler.ts, src/workflow/code-review/grounding.ts]","action":"Keep unsuccessful selected files distinguishable from fresh files and route incomplete grounding to degraded review. Add a mixed-set regression with one indexed file and one failed index request.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Entity-less files currently use repoLastIndexed, and the freshness handler does not request indexing.","evidence":"computeCodeReviewFreshness reads repoLastIndexed lazily and applies 'if (repoLastIndexed < mtime) staleFiles.push(file)'. The complete codeReview.freshness handler supplies read seams and returns the result without enqueueing. Analyzer output resolved an unrelated Kotlin target, so verification continued through direct file reads. [files: src/workflow/code-review/freshness.ts, src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts]","action":"Retain this root-cause description.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"An ordinary Markdown file is not held by the index and selectFile returns not-code for it.","evidence":"ArtifactParser.extensions includes '.md' and '.mdx'; artifact.ts calls 'registerParser(artifactParser)'. Its parse method creates a File entity and document/section entities. selectFile returns selected for a small, nonignored Markdown file. The proposed real-seam integration test therefore expects the wrong result. [files: src/indexer/parser/artifact.ts, src/indexer/parser/registry.ts, src/indexer/file-selection.ts, src/indexer/index.ts]","action":"Use an unsupported extension for the not-code fixture. Expect ordinary Markdown to be selected, and correct the edge-case and test descriptions.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The listed FreshnessResult consumer sites accurately identify the affected contract.","evidence":"code-review-rpc.ts:248-255 belongs to parseFallbackReason and validates a CodeReviewFallbackReason, including 'Object.keys(r).length === 5'. It does not consume FreshnessResult. The actual freshness producer is freshness.ts, composed by handler-runtime.ts; the controller consumes freshness separately in handler.ts. [files: src/daemon/code-review-rpc.ts, src/workflow/code-review/freshness.ts, src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts, src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/handler.ts]","action":"Remove code-review-rpc.ts from the FreshnessResult call-site list and distinguish fallback-reason compatibility checks from freshness-result consumers.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.1","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Queued or running file jobs count as repo code-index work, and queued jobs for an identical path are replaced.","evidence":"codeIndexWorkFor includes full/reconcile jobs naming the repo and file jobs under its path, reading both lane.inFlight and lane.jobs. enqueue finds an existing queued file job by exact filePath and executes 'queue[idx] = job'. The controller waits while isProcessing is true or staleFiles is nonempty. [files: src/daemon/queue.ts, src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/handler.ts]","action":"Normalize map and enqueue paths consistently to absolute paths so equivalent input spellings use the same key.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.2","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed entity-present rule and unchanged controller preserve watermark comparison and bounded timeout behavior.","evidence":"The existing entity branch marks stale only when 'watermark < mtime'. The controller computes a deadline using freshnessTimeoutMs and calls beginDiffOnlyReview with kind 'freshness-timeout' when it expires. The design explicitly leaves both branches unchanged. [files: src/workflow/code-review/freshness.ts, src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/handler.ts]","action":"Retain regression coverage for entity watermarks and timeout fallback.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.3","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The linked sequence companion renders consistently with the proposed interaction.","evidence":"Inspected sequence-diagram.html source: it contains five participants, eight messages, descriptions, and bundled Mermaid code. No rendered browser view was obtained, so layout and successful Mermaid rendering remain unverified. Source also says 'isProcessing becomes true once the job is queued', whereas the proposed handler returns a compute result sampled before enqueueing. [files: docs/standalone/fix-code-review-freshness-gate-so-E20261027fa396bdf/S001/sequence-diagram.html, src/workflow/code-review/freshness.ts]","action":"Render the companion and verify readability; clarify that queue processing appears on a subsequent freshness sample, or explicitly refresh the returned queue fields.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The acceptance mapping fully proves the approved ISSUE's fix intent.","evidence":"The proposed tests cover classification, request deduplication, mtime changes and attempted-idle completion, but none verifies degraded review after an unsuccessful request in a mixed changed set. Existing handler tests exercise globally empty grounding via '{ symbols: [] }', which cannot catch partial grounding. Existing freshness tests also assert complete result objects without unindexedFiles and will need updates when the field is added. [files: docs/standalone/fix-code-review-freshness-gate-so-E20261027fa396bdf/ISSUE.md, src/workflow/code-review/__tests__/freshness.test.ts, src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/__tests__/handler.test.ts, src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/handler.ts]","action":"Add a regression connecting unsuccessful indexing to degraded review with another changed file successfully grounded. Update existing freshness result assertions and correct the Markdown integration expectation. Preserve the separate handler/RPC suites as planned.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"}],"counts":{"high":2,"med":2,"low":4,"unverified":1},"template":"design-issue","reviewedAt":"2026-10-27T06:00:03.188Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
