8509	{"artifactId":"LLD-fa396bdf197b8e8b-s1","entry":{"id":"review-e52fe0e1a47841beae628b10a762d635","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-27T06:06:07.855Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.1","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Classification plus file-index requests addresses the ISSUE's entity-less-file freshness defect.","evidence":"ISSUE.md requires indexable changed files to become fresh without a full reindex and excluded files not to block. freshness.ts currently uses `if (repoLastIndexed < mtime) staleFiles.push(file)` for entity-less files; handler-runtime.ts queues nothing in codeReview.freshness. Indexer.fileEvent processes update jobs through indexFile, and the TypeScript and Markdown parsers create File entities. The proposed classification/request mechanism addresses these causes. [files: docs/standalone/fix-code-review-freshness-gate-so-E20261027fa396bdf/ISSUE.md, src/workflow/code-review/freshness.ts, src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts, src/indexer/index.ts, src/indexer/parser/typescript.ts, src/indexer/parser/artifact.ts]","action":"Retain this approach, subject to the deleted-file correction below.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing compute uses the entity watermark when available and otherwise the repo watermark; the freshness handler is read-only.","evidence":"The complete compute branches on `watermark !== null`, compares that watermark with mtime, and otherwise lazily reads repoLastIndexed. The complete codeReview.freshness handler supplies graph and queue read seams and returns the result without enqueueing. [files: src/workflow/code-review/freshness.ts, src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Repo lastIndexed advances only when a full index completes.","evidence":"Indexer startup also advances it after enqueueing incremental delta jobs: `for (const filePath of delta) { this.queue.enqueue({ kind: 'file', filePath, event: 'update' }); }` followed by `await updateRepoStatus(this.db, repo.path, 'ready', new Date().toISOString());`. This happens before those jobs complete. [files: src/indexer/index.ts, docs/standalone/fix-code-review-freshness-gate-so-E20261027fa396bdf/S001/LLD.md]","action":"Correct the migration/current-behavior explanation. Include the startup delta writer when explaining why repo lastIndexed cannot establish per-file freshness.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed production changes are localized to the freshness compute/real seams and daemon freshness handler; existing controller reply consumers need no field addition.","evidence":"Source search located the production compute call in handler-runtime.ts and the real seam implementation in freshness.ts. shared/review-stream.ts constructs a CodeReviewFreshnessResult from the four existing fields, discarding additional reply fields. The controller uses that result rather than FreshnessResult directly. Indexer imports register the language parsers, and resolveRepoIgnore provides the proposed selection configuration. [files: src/workflow/code-review/freshness.ts, src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts, src/shared/review-stream.ts, src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/handler.ts, src/indexer/index.ts, src/indexer/repo-ignore-config.ts]","action":"Keep absolute-path normalization consistent between selection, request-map lookup, and enqueueing.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.1","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Deleted or unstattable changed files remain non-stale under the proposed rules.","evidence":"fileMtime catches stat failures and returns 0. selectFile classifies a missing .ts path as `selected`: parser lookup succeeds and it performs no existence check for this parser. The proposed postcondition says an entity-less selected file is always stale, so a deleted .ts file would remain stale and be requested despite the edge-case promise. Indexer.indexFile catches the missing-file read and returns false, leaving it stale until timeout. [files: src/workflow/code-review/freshness.ts, src/indexer/file-selection.ts, src/indexer/index.ts, docs/standalone/fix-code-review-freshness-gate-so-E20261027fa396bdf/S001/LLD.md]","action":"Explicitly handle mtime 0 before the entity-less selection/request branch. Add deleted-source and stat-failure regression cases proving neither staleness nor an index request is introduced.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.2","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Queue accounting, queued-file replacement, and the bounded degraded-review fallback support the proposed behavior.","evidence":"IndexQueue.codeIndexWorkFor counts queued/running file jobs under the repo; enqueue replaces a queued file job with the same filePath. The controller waits while processing or stale files remain, then calls beginDiffOnlyReview at its deadline. assembleCodeReviewGrounding emits rows only for returned entities, while the full-review hollow check is `g.grounding.symbols.length === 0`, confirming why a failed file in a mixed set must remain stale. [files: src/daemon/queue.ts, src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/handler.ts, src/workflow/code-review/grounding.ts]","action":"Preserve these branches and existing reply-field meanings.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.3","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The linked sequence companion renders consistently with the proposed interaction.","evidence":"Inspected sequence-diagram.html: its Mermaid source includes the gate, handler, compute, queue, indexer, enqueue, queue re-read, and subsequent poll. The prose specifies request-map ownership, per-file requests, and additive compatibility; no ERD or UX mock is necessary for this transient-state change. Attempting to open the companion returned `Browser is not available: iab`, so rendering, clipping, and visual legibility were not verified. [files: docs/standalone/fix-code-review-freshness-gate-so-E20261027fa396bdf/S001/sequence-diagram.html, docs/standalone/fix-code-review-freshness-gate-so-E20261027fa396bdf/S001/LLD.md]","action":"Render the existing companion and verify diagram readability and consistency before approval.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed acceptance mapping provides meaningful regression coverage for ac1–ac5.","evidence":"Against the current compute and handler, the planned selected-file request, excluded-file classification, request suppression/re-request, and post-enqueue queue-state assertions would expose the missing behavior. Existing freshness tests cover watermark comparisons and complete result objects; existing handler tests already exercise timeout-to-diff fallback. The proposed mixed-set contract test strengthens that coverage. These are planned tests, not implemented or executed evidence; unchanged fallback tests serve preservation rather than detecting the new fix. [files: src/workflow/code-review/__tests__/freshness.test.ts, src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/__tests__/handler.test.ts, src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts, docs/standalone/fix-code-review-freshness-gate-so-E20261027fa396bdf/S001/LLD.md]","action":"Implement the mapped tests and add the deleted/unstattable cases identified above. Run the named regression suites.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":1,"med":1,"low":6,"unverified":1},"template":"design-issue","reviewedAt":"2026-10-27T06:06:07.855Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
