6369	{"artifactId":"LLD-fa396bdf197b8e8b-s1","entry":{"id":"review-dc9110e3d39ec7878b4a31e98e1ea51b","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-27T06:11:42.411Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.1","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The proposed requests cover the approved ISSUE's requirement to request stale changed files when the queue is idle.","evidence":"ISSUE.md says: \"when files are stale and the queue is idle, the wait asks for those changed files to be indexed\". The LLD explicitly excludes files with existing entities from unindexedFiles and requests. computeCodeReviewFreshness currently marks an existing-entity file stale when \"watermark < mtime\"; the controller only polls. Thus an indexed source file whose update the watcher missed still receives no indexing request and unnecessarily reaches degraded review. [files: docs/standalone/fix-code-review-freshness-gate-so-E20261027fa396bdf/ISSUE.md, src/workflow/code-review/freshness.ts, src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/handler.ts]","action":"Request indexing once per mtime for stale selected files with outdated entities too, while preserving their watermark comparison; add an idle-queue missed-update regression test.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Entity-less freshness currently depends on the repo watermark, and freshness polling does not request indexing.","evidence":"The compute lazily reads repoLastIndexed and applies \"if (repoLastIndexed < mtime) staleFiles.push(file)\". The complete codeReview.freshness handler supplies graph, queue and repo reads and returns the compute result without enqueueing. Indexer startup advances lastIndexed immediately after enqueueing delta file jobs. [files: src/workflow/code-review/freshness.ts, src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts, src/indexer/index.ts]","action":"Replace this fallback as proposed.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed production changes cover the freshness producer and its typed consumers without requiring a client protocol change.","evidence":"Repository-wide symbol searches locate the compute's production caller in handler-runtime.ts and its FreshnessDeps fixtures in freshness.test.ts. freshnessFromReply explicitly copies isProcessing, inFlight, pendingCodeIndexJobs and staleFiles, so an additional reply field is ignored. selectFile and parser-registration imports exist in the stated indexer modules. [files: src/workflow/code-review/freshness.ts, src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts, src/workflow/code-review/__tests__/freshness.test.ts, src/shared/review-stream.ts, src/indexer/file-selection.ts, src/indexer/index.ts]","action":"Use absolute paths consistently for queue jobs and request-map keys, as the design specifies.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.1","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing queue signal and bounded degraded-review fallback can remain unchanged.","evidence":"IndexQueue.codeIndexWorkFor counts queued and running file jobs under the repo; enqueue replaces a queued file job with the same filePath. The controller breaks only when processing is false and staleFiles is empty, and on deadline calls beginDiffOnlyReview with kind 'freshness-timeout'. Successful grounding falls back for hollow grounding only when \"symbols.length === 0\". [files: src/daemon/queue.ts, src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/handler.ts]","action":"Preserve these branches and re-sample queue state after enqueueing as proposed.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.2","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The linked sequence companion renders consistently with the proposed interactions.","evidence":"Inspected the generated HTML's Mermaid source: it shows handler → compute, handler → queue, queue → indexer, and a later poll returning fresh or still stale. The prose adequately describes request-map ownership and additive IPC compatibility; no ERD or UX mock is necessary. Browser rendering was not verified; local playwright and puppeteer packages are unavailable. [files: docs/standalone/fix-code-review-freshness-gate-so-E20261027fa396bdf/S001/sequence-diagram.html]","action":"Render the existing companion and verify legibility and consistency before approval; no reviewer-authored replacement is needed.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed test strategy covers the LLD's ac1–ac5 with meaningful regression assertions.","evidence":"The existing freshness suite asserts repo-watermark exclusion and exact result objects. Proposed tests replace that behavior with selection-based exclusion, request suppression per mtime, re-request after edits, and immediate queue-state reporting; these new behavior assertions fail against current code. Existing handler tests already exercise timeout fallback, and the proposed mixed-set test adds explicit protection against full review with an unindexed file. These are planned tests, not verified passing implementations. [files: src/workflow/code-review/__tests__/freshness.test.ts, src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/__tests__/handler.test.ts, docs/standalone/fix-code-review-freshness-gate-so-E20261027fa396bdf/S001/LLD.md]","action":"Implement the mapped tests and add the outdated-existing-entity case identified under fix-targets-defect. Keep preservation tests even where they already pass without the fix.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":1,"med":0,"low":5,"unverified":1},"template":"design-issue","reviewedAt":"2026-10-27T06:11:42.411Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
