7678	{"artifactId":"LLD-fa396bdf197b8e8b-s1","entry":{"id":"review-fe3ec081db71a0b43888b8fce4ec19d5","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-27T06:23:09.385Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"warn","summary":"review: warn","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"warn","findings":[{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.1","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Classification and incremental index requests address the approved ISSUE while unsuccessful indexing remains stale until degraded review.","evidence":"ISSUE.md requires freshness without full reindex and degraded review when indexing fails. The current compute uses 'if (repoLastIndexed < mtime) staleFiles.push(file)' for entity-less files, and the freshness handler queues nothing. Indexer.fileEvent handles update jobs through indexFile(..., true), which deletes old entities and persists parsed entities. Keeping failed files stale preserves the controller's 'freshness-timeout' fallback before grounding. The analyzer returned incomplete implementation evidence; these conclusions were checked through file reads. [files: docs/standalone/fix-code-review-freshness-gate-so-E20261027fa396bdf/ISSUE.md, src/workflow/code-review/freshness.ts, src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts, src/indexer/index.ts, src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/handler.ts]","action":"Retain the proposed classification, request and persistent-staleness rules.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Current freshness uses entity watermarks or the repo fallback, and startup can advance the repo watermark before delta jobs finish.","evidence":"The complete compute compares 'watermark < mtime', otherwise lazily reads repoLastIndexed. fileMtime catches stat failures and returns 0. Startup enqueues delta file updates and then calls updateRepoStatus(..., 'ready', new Date().toISOString()). The complete freshness handler supplies read seams and returns the compute result without enqueueing. [files: src/workflow/code-review/freshness.ts, src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts, src/indexer/index.ts]","action":"Retain this corrected root-cause account.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed production changes cover the freshness computation, real seams and daemon request orchestration without requiring controller contract changes.","evidence":"Repository-wide searches locate the compute's production caller in handler-runtime.ts and its injectable fixtures in freshness.test.ts. The real seam also has a DB-test caller, which reads its existing fields. freshnessFromReply constructs a result using only isProcessing, inFlight, pendingCodeIndexJobs and staleFiles, so the additive field requires no consumer change. selectFile already implements parser, generated-file, artifact-size, lockfile and ignore classification. [files: src/workflow/code-review/freshness.ts, src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts, src/indexer/file-selection.ts, src/shared/review-stream.ts, src/db/__tests__/entity-scope-indexes.test.ts, src/workflow/code-review/__tests__/freshness.test.ts]","action":"Use one normalized absolute path for both request-map keys and queued jobs; queue deduplication compares exact path strings.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.1","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Queue accounting, queued-file replacement and bounded degraded fallback support the proposed behavior.","evidence":"codeIndexWorkFor counts running and queued file jobs under the repo, plus full/reconcile jobs. enqueue replaces an existing queued file entry with 'queue[idx] = job'. The controller waits while processing or stale files remain and invokes beginDiffOnlyReview when its freshness deadline expires. Its later hollow-grounding fallback checks only 'g.grounding.symbols.length === 0'; retaining staleness for a failed file therefore protects mixed changed sets. [files: src/daemon/queue.ts, src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/handler.ts, src/workflow/code-review/grounding.ts]","action":"Preserve these branches and the mixed-set timeout regression.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.2","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed interaction and process-local map ownership are adequately documented in prose and companion source.","evidence":"The design specifies one absolute-path-to-request-time map owned by the daemon handler closure, process lifetime, restart behavior and additive IPC compatibility. The linked companion contains five participants and nine messages covering compute, enqueue, queue re-read and subsequent polling, consistent with the design. No persistent entity relationship change requires an ERD. [files: docs/standalone/fix-code-review-freshness-gate-so-E20261027fa396bdf/S001/LLD.md, docs/standalone/fix-code-review-freshness-gate-so-E20261027fa396bdf/S001/sequence-diagram.html]","action":"Retain the ownership and compatibility documentation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.3","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The generated sequence companion renders successfully and readably.","evidence":"Inspected the generated HTML's Mermaid sequence source, participant descriptions and message table. Attempted to open the local companion with the browser tool; it returned 'Browser is not available: iab'. Successful rendering and visual layout were not verified. [files: docs/standalone/fix-code-review-freshness-gate-so-E20261027fa396bdf/S001/sequence-diagram.html]","action":"Render the existing companion and verify diagram visibility, readability and consistency before claiming visual verification.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The planned tests provide regression coverage for all six LLD acceptance criteria.","evidence":"The acceptance mapping covers selected entity-less files, exclusions/deletion, request suppression without false freshness, preserved watermarks, post-enqueue queue sampling and missed updates. Existing freshness tests demonstrate the old repo-fallback behavior and exact result assertions. Proposed selection and enqueue tests would fail against that implementation. The planned mixed-set stale-file timeout test checks the critical degraded-review path independently of globally empty grounding. [files: docs/standalone/fix-code-review-freshness-gate-so-E20261027fa396bdf/S001/LLD.md, src/workflow/code-review/__tests__/freshness.test.ts, src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/handler.ts, src/indexer/parser/artifact.ts]","action":"Implement the proposed tests. Update existing README.md entity-less fixtures and their comments to distinguish selected Markdown from unsupported files; adding unindexedFiles to exact assertions alone is insufficient. This assesses test design, not completed or passing tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":7,"unverified":1},"template":"design-issue","reviewedAt":"2026-10-27T06:23:09.385Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
