8017	{"artifactId":"LLD-fa396bdf197b8e8b-s1","entry":{"id":"review-904267914ada54e86187d9a70fdee93d","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-27T07:31:41.902Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"warn","summary":"review: warn","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"warn","findings":[{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.1","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Selection-based classification, explicit file jobs, and retaining staleness after a request address the ISSUE's fix intent.","evidence":"The ISSUE requires freshness without a full reindex, exclusion of files the index never holds, and degraded review when indexing cannot recover. Currently computeCodeReviewFreshness uses 'if (repoLastIndexed < mtime) staleFiles.push(file)' for entity-less files; codeReview.freshness only returns that compute's result. The proposed changes replace that fallback and request the existing incremental indexing path while retaining the timeout escape. [files: docs/standalone/fix-code-review-freshness-gate-so-E20261027fa396bdf/ISSUE.md, src/workflow/code-review/freshness.ts, src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts, src/indexer/index.ts]","action":"Proceed with this approach. The LLD explicitly identifies the ISSUE's inaccurate timeout explanation; reconcile the ISSUE for traceability.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing Linux watcher can miss descendants created before their parent's watch is installed.","evidence":"Watcher.addRepo forwards backend events without scanning created directories. InotifyBackend::subscribe recursively watches the initial tree, but handleSubscription handles a new directory with only 'watchDir(watcher, path, sub->tree)'; it does not recursively discover existing descendants. This supports the stated nested-directory race, though it does not establish that every mkdir -p invocation must trigger it. [files: src/indexer/watcher.ts, node_modules/@parcel/watcher/src/linux/InotifyBackend.cc]","action":"Describe the Linux failure as timing-dependent rather than unconditional.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The freshness wait already times out into degraded diff review, and full grounding falls back only when its symbol set is empty.","evidence":"The resumed loop checks 'deps.now() >= deadline' and calls beginDiffOnlyReview with kind 'freshness-timeout'. After successful grounding, the hollow fallback checks 'g.grounding.symbols.length === 0'. A partially grounded changed set therefore needs to remain stale to avoid full review without the missing file. [files: src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/handler.ts]","action":"Preserve these branches as proposed.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed production change sites cover the watcher lifecycle, freshness computation, real selection seam, and queue-producing IPC handler without requiring a consumer protocol change.","evidence":"Watcher owns subscriptions in addRepo/removeRepo/close. The freshness compute and real seams reside together in freshness.ts, and handler-runtime supplies queue and repo seams. Repository-wide reference search found no additional production FreshnessDeps constructors requiring new fields. freshnessFromReply explicitly projects the existing fields, so an additive unindexedFiles reply does not require controller changes. [files: src/indexer/watcher.ts, src/workflow/code-review/freshness.ts, src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts, src/shared/review-stream.ts, src/workflow/code-review/__tests__/freshness.test.ts]","action":"Keep the new result field internal to the daemon request logic; update the existing FreshnessDeps test fixtures as specified.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The linked sequence companion renders consistently with the proposed interactions.","evidence":"Inspected the actual HTML, Mermaid sequence source, participant/message descriptions, embedded renderer, and initialization code. The source depicts subscribe-before-scan and enqueue-before-queue-reread consistently with the LLD. Attempting to open the companion returned 'Browser is not available: iab', so rendering, clipping, and legibility could not be verified. Subscription ownership and lifecycle are adequately described in prose; no ERD is necessary for these in-memory maps. [files: docs/standalone/fix-code-review-freshness-gate-so-E20261027fa396bdf/S001/sequence-diagram.html]","action":"Render the existing companion in an available browser and verify its diagram and viewport before claiming visual verification.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.1","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing event shape, queued-file replacement, indexed-file watermark rule, and consumer field meanings can be preserved by the proposed additive changes.","evidence":"Watcher emits {type,path} through a 200 ms debounce. IndexQueue.enqueue replaces a pending file job using exact filePath equality: 'queue[idx] = job'. The compute compares entity watermark < mtime, and freshnessFromReply copies the existing processing and stale-file fields. fileEvent invokes indexFile with cleanFirst=true, which deletes old relations/entities before parsing and persisting replacements. Deduplication covers pending jobs, not work already in flight, so the claim that duplicate events 'cost nothing' is overstated. [files: src/indexer/watcher.ts, src/daemon/queue.ts, src/workflow/code-review/freshness.ts, src/indexer/index.ts, src/shared/review-stream.ts]","action":"Preserve these contracts and normalize requested paths to absolute paths. Qualify the duplicate-event claim: pending jobs coalesce, but duplicates can still cause additional indexing.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The planned acceptance mapping exercises the changed decisions and recovery paths with regressions that distinguish the fix from current code.","evidence":"Existing freshness tests encode repo-watermark fallback and whole-result assertions. The proposed selection/request tests distinguish that behavior from selected entity-less files remaining stale, excluded files settling, and stale indexed files requesting recovery. Handler integration tests cover request suppression, renewed requests after mtime changes, and queue-state rereads. Watcher tests cover initial nested files and later writes, ignore rules, deletion/recreation, and cleanup. The timeout branch already exists, so its contract test preserves behavior rather than independently demonstrating the fix. These are planned tests, not implemented or executed evidence. [files: src/workflow/code-review/__tests__/freshness.test.ts, src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/__tests__/handler.test.ts, src/indexer/watcher.ts, docs/standalone/fix-code-review-freshness-gate-so-E20261027fa396bdf/S001/LLD.md]","action":"Implement the mapped tests. Also consider injecting a rejected per-directory subscription to verify the promised scan-after-subscribe-failure path; the unreadable-directory test does not exercise that branch.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":7,"unverified":1},"template":"design-issue","reviewedAt":"2026-10-27T07:31:41.902Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
